message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the associated paper (the preferred
  citation below). To reference a specific archived code version, also cite the
  Zenodo DOI for that release.
title: LLMSmokeDetector
abstract: >-
  A two-stage large language model pipeline for extracting tobacco smoking
  status (Smoker, Never smoker, Unknown) from free-text clinical discharge
  summaries, with evaluation utilities that compute multiclass and per-class
  metrics, bootstrap confidence intervals, and confusion matrices. Companion
  code for a JAMIA Open Brief Communication comparing lightweight open-source
  large language models against the cTAKES NLP system.
